So here's Sucky Suckington III (yes, I do have a thing for stupid
names) the lawful human Valkyrie, doing good but not great.  Got
Mjollnir and Frost Brand proofed, blessed and up to +6, a
respectable-sized stash next to an altar, blessed unicorn horn and bag
of holding, all the standard resistances, amulet of ESP, plenty of
protection, GDSM and reflect shield, with ~150 HP and an AC in the low
(high?) -10s.  However, she didn't have any other kit armor, although
she did have a blessed, apparently rustproof, +6 helmet (I swear it was
like that when I found it.)  More importantly, I hadn't found any
wishes yet, and although I had two magic markers and some blanks, I
hadn't identified genocide.  Although the thought of rust monsters,
liches and master mind flayers creeping around scared me a bit, I
should've been worried about another letter altogether.  But now I'm
getting ahead of myself (albeit not by much.)
So there I was at the castle.  Having cleaned out a swamp a few levels
earlier, I felt confident enough to tidy up the moat a bit.  I stabbed
a few sharks, then saw a giant eel coming.  No problem, I thought, I
have this handy little ring of free action on.
The eel swung around me and I said, "wate wut?"  But I wasn't about to
panic just yet--well, maybe a little.  I flipped open my inventory and
hoped I had something useful that wasn't stashed.  Ah, wand of
teleportation, good.  What do you want to zap?  This one, please.
Which direction?  Thataway.  Sayonara, sucker--

DYWYPI?

